## [fix: query GL_MAX_SAMPLES before setting multisampling hint](https://github.com/MonoGame/MonoGame/pull/8087)

> > If the OpenGL driver cannot handle it is will use the maximum value it can.
> 
> Unfortunately the GL driver doesn't intelligently do this, and that causes the crash that this PR is meant to prevent.
> 
> > We can leave the code to call `SetAttribute` as it is now since it is only a `hint`.
> 
> It may be called a hint, but it's not treated as something optional. The `SetAttribute()` call with an invalid `GL_SAMPLES` value will cause the context creation that happens after it to fail. `GL_SAMPLES` (abstracted as `SDL_GL_MULTISAMPLESAMPLES`) must be set to a value supported by the driver before context creation, and changing it requires re-creating the context.
> 
> `Sdl.GL.GetAttribute()` would call `glGetIntegerv()` which cannot be used without a current valid GL context, which will fail to be created if `GL_MAX_SAMPLES` is set too high. The hidden dummy window being created would have the default `GL_MAX_SAMPLES` value of `0` which would allow it to be safely created in order to poll the `GL_MAX_SAMPLES` value in order to limit it.
> 
> Note that SDL2 does not expose `GL_MAX_SAMPLES` via `SDL_GL_GetAttribute()`, GL must be queried directly.
