> Because the NSWindow exception was indirectly triggering the test failure, I simply removed it. The only reason I had originally added exceptions was to bubble up the real platform errors during initialization, but that particular SDL window creation doesn't include GL, so throwing `NoSuitableGraphicsDeviceException` from there was not really necessary.
> 
> Also while investigating the failures I did eventually notice that my assumption that the `GraphicsDeviceManagerTest` tests were passing was in fact _not correct_ because they appear to never be executed at all. The class is not included in the workflow file at all. I do not know if that is intentional.
